## Commits
### e9bc6cd
test(state): add array push/pop benchmark on both kinds of state

Measure the pattern the wrap-array-methods-on-hookless-state change
alters: one effect subscribed to a reactive array's length, then a loop
of push followed by pop, timed like the effect triggers case. Run it
once on hookless state and once on state created with no-op onRead and
onWrite hooks so the two code paths get separate figures.

The library is unchanged in this commit, so the numbers this run
records are the baseline later tickets compare against.


